                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 24 at 12:53AM CDT until September 24 at 5:00AM CDT by NWS Dodge City KS",
                "description": "FFWDDC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Dodge City has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorthwestern Grant County in southwestern Kansas...\nSoutheastern Hamilton County in southwestern Kansas...\nWestern Kearny County in southwestern Kansas...\nNortheastern Morton County in southwestern Kansas...\nEastern Stanton County in southwestern Kansas...\n\n* Until 500 AM CDT /400 AM MDT/.\n\n* At 1253 AM CDT /1153 PM MDT/, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms\nproducing heavy rain across the warned area. Between 2 and 3 inches\nof rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches\nare possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nUlysses, Kendall and Big Bow.",
